This product includes a deployment-only extraction of Florence-2 (Bin Xiao et al.,
"Florence-2: Advancing a Unified Representation for a Variety of Vision Tasks",
arXiv:2311.06242). Microsoft publishes Florence-2 only as Hugging Face model
repositories (huggingface.co/microsoft/Florence-2-base and siblings) that carry
their own implementation -- modeling_florence2.py, processing_florence2.py,
configuration_florence2.py -- under the MIT License in each repository's LICENSE
file. vision.py, language.py, network.py, image.py, tokenizer.py, parse.py and
config.py derive from those files; see LICENSE, which is byte-identical to the
LICENSE file of microsoft/Florence-2-base at commit 5ca5edf5.

decoding.py transcribes the beam search, logits processors, stopping criteria and
compute_transition_scores of the transformers library, version 4.53.3:

  - transformers
    Copyright 2020 The HuggingFace Inc. team.
    https://github.com/huggingface/transformers
    Apache License, Version 2.0 -- see LICENSE.Apache-2.0

The vocabulary in assets/florence2_vocab.json.gz is derived from tokenizer.json in
microsoft/Florence-2-base (BART's byte-level BPE, originally Facebook AI's, as
redistributed there under the repository's MIT terms) plus the 1,024 tokens
Florence2Processor adds at load.

The model weights are licensed separately from this code, and identically: each
of the four Microsoft repositories states `license: mit` on its model card and
carries the MIT LICENSE file. mozo publishes them with that file and a NOTICE.

NOT INCLUDED
------------
Every Florence-2 task other than <OD> and <OCR_WITH_REGION> (captioning, plain
OCR, phrase grounding, open-vocabulary detection, dense region captions, region
proposals, referring and region segmentation, region-to-text), sampling, the
training code, flash attention, and transformers' native Florence2 port. See
PROVENANCE.md.
